    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:75`), alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger.\n\n2. **Enqueued the welcome notification on successful create** \u2014 after the owner is persisted and audited in `createOwner(...)`, a new `enqueueWelcomeNotification(owner)` call emits an info line on the `NOTIFY` logger:\n   ```\n   welcome owner id={} memberId={}\n   ```\n   containing both the owner id and the unified `memberId`.\n\nThe line is emitted only on the successful-create path (after `saveOwner`), so failed creates (400/409/429) don't notify. `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and its `memberId` \u2014 passes, as does the full suite.",
